# Debug the running app

`npm run tauri dev` serves Vite at `http://localhost:1420` and opens a WKWebView. WKWebView has no Chrome DevTools Protocol. Browser tools on port 1420 are not the desktop window: `isTauri()` is false and scans will not run.

Use the debug-only MCP bridge (`tauri-plugin-mcp-bridge`, `127.0.0.1:9223`, permission `mcp-bridge:default`). It is off in release builds. Cursor loads it from `.cursor/mcp.json`. From the shell:

```bash
npx -y -p @hypothesi/tauri-mcp-cli tauri-mcp driver-session start --port 9223
npx -y -p @hypothesi/tauri-mcp-cli tauri-mcp webview-screenshot --file /tmp/dev-doctor.png
npx -y -p @hypothesi/tauri-mcp-cli tauri-mcp webview-execute-js --script '(() => document.title)()'
```

UI work is unfinished until this session is used. Start it once per `tauri dev` process, then screenshot and read the image. For a click or toggle, run `webview-interact` and screenshot again. Compare native buttons from `window_chrome` with the toggle `getBoundingClientRect()` when chrome spacing changes.

```bash
npx -y -p @hypothesi/tauri-mcp-cli tauri-mcp webview-interact --action click --selector '[aria-pressed]'
```

Do not add an in-app layout harness overlay. Dashed boxes and a measurement panel were tried and rejected.

